PKG=gayle30
NAME=gayle-k30 1.1.0-6 - A4000 Gayle IDE driver module (root class), k30 line
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.1.0-6
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none
VENDOR=amix
PSTAMP=amix-gayle30-1.1.0-6
# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2, C3-5 v9 sec 1, C4-2): a role=module entry of
# the #ext kpkg block (line=k30, kabi=k30.1.2), class root, never an ordinary
# entry.  Catalog name gayle-k30, pkginst gayle30; VERSION is the package's:
# 1.1.0-6 is the module's 1.1.0-3 (the fork's module/VERSION at
# kernel/drivers/gayle-ide/gayle-ide.pin), its object built with the
# gcc-2.7.2.3-33ebadc kit, rolled from amix.
APKG_DESC=A4000 Gayle IDE as a root-class kernel module for the 68030 root-class module kernel kernel-k30-m (kabi k30.1.2): /etc/conf/mod.d/gayle, interrupt I/O by default (param intr=0: polled).
DESC=The amix-gayle-ide driver built as an amix-dlm kernel module for the 68030 line (kabi k30.1.2): root class, loaded by the module core's root pass before the root filesystem is mounted on an A4000 (match mobo:gayle), the IDE port registered with sd at rank ide as a pseudo SCSI host adapter; never unloaded.  Interrupt I/O by default (intr=1): at the first sysinit the module attaches INT2 and self-tests with one READ VERIFY, and stays polled if the test fails; the line param intr=0 in /etc/conf/modreg.local.d/gayle selects polled I/O.  No major and no device nodes of its own: sd owns the disk majors and nodes.  /etc/conf/modreg.d/gayle holds the package's defaults (none; comments only).  The package writes no boot store; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).  MIT.
